          "create_time": 1792521000.712,
          "update_time": 1792521002.894,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The main distinction is whether RH is assumed. A multiple zero at \\(t=0\\) fits the local heat-flow geometry, but the current “force a later collision” argument needs all zeros to be real at later times. I’m separating an unconditional simplicity track from a track conditional on RH, and checking the higher-multiplicity cases too."
            ]
          },
