          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Understood—the goal is to prove simplicity on the critical line independently of RH. That makes forcing a later collision insufficient on its own: we need either a direct contradiction at \\(t=0\\), or a stronger consequence that conflicts with something known unconditionally. I’ll center the note on those possibilities."
